cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use T9Sim v2.2, please cite it as below."
title: "T9Sim v2.2: A Censored-View Auction Simulator for Measuring the Marginal Value of AdTech Data Layers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yu"
    given-names: "Ken Kanghsu"
    affiliation: "Queen Mary University of London"
  - family-names: "Klimis"
    given-names: "Vasileios"
    affiliation: "Queen Mary University of London"
version: 2.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/QUMLKY/T9Sim-v2"
abstract: >
  T9Sim v2.2 generates a synthetic mobile-game ad-auction ground truth and censors it into four
  views (C1 DSP, C2 DSP+MMP, C3 DSP+SSP, C4 all), so that the marginal predictive and economic
  value of each integrated AdTech data layer can be measured as a controlled ablation. MMP adds
  rows and SSP adds columns, over one shared master with one temporal split, so every contrast is
  paired within a seed. The funnel heads receive every supply-side feature while their labels are
  identical across views, and the interval-censored AFT price head has identical features across
  views while its labels differ, so a supply-side effect is separated into a feature channel and a
  label channel rather than reported as a single number. It is an independent rebuild sharing no
  code with T9Sim v1, and it supersedes v2.0, which was never released.
keywords:
  - real-time bidding
  - computational advertising
  - synthetic data
  - selection bias
  - ablation study
license: MIT
